Usage: agent-deck open <file|url> [--session <id|title>] [--json] [--browser-profile <name>] [--wait <duration>]
       agent-deck open --last --session <id|title> [--json]
       agent-deck open --list --session <id|title> --json
       agent-deck open --show <page-id> --session <id|title> [--json]
  -browser-profile string
    	Browser panel profile in the app (optional; letters, digits, '.', '_', '-', at most 64, no leading '.')
  -json
    	print one JSON object: {status, where, session, title, path, url, page_id, page_title, name, kind, phone, elapsed_ms}
  -last
    	open the newest page this session opened again (exit 2 when it has none)
  -list
    	list the pages this session opened, newest first (with --json)
  -session string
    	session id or title (default: $AGENTDECK_INSTANCE_ID, then the calling tmux session)
  -show string
    	print one opened page as a self-contained HTML document (--json: with metadata)
  -wait duration
    	how long to wait for the app to acknowledge before reporting Queued (at most 2m0s) (default 3s)
